  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Heightened wildfire spread risk this afternoon\n\nCoordinated special weather statement with PA\nDCNR and WFOs BGM/PHI was issued this morning for elevated \nwildfire spread risk. While minRH values remain somewhat \nmarginal, gusty NW winds 20-30 mph and excessively dry \nconditions over the past 2 weeks are driving the heightened \nwildfire threat for the remainder of the afternoon. \n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Lengthy run of dry and mild weather continues \ninto early November before coming to an end by late next week \n\nAnother very pleasant and comfortable weekend to close out \nOctober (Halloween) and start November (ending daylight saving \ntime). \n\nThe latest model guidance continues to grow in agreement with \nthe progression of a CONUS-crossing upper trough eventually \nreaching the eastern U.S. by the second half of next week.\nHighest odds for rain are currently placed around Thursday \n11/5. There also continues to be some indications that rich \nGulf moisture will be pulled northward along a well defined \nnorth south oriented frontal zone accompanying the full \nlatitude upper trough which could result in moderate to heavy \nrainfall.",
